IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition: the CORE.
-- Nouns only: DECLARE and two dated constants. No rule is written here.
-- Every part of the Act imports this module and reads it, never edits it.
-- A part that lacks a type or constructor defines its own under its own provision label
-- (s 76B(1)(a) ..., sch 13 para 2 ...) and records it in NEEDS-CORE.md; the lead hoists it at the merge.
--
-- Conventions the whole family follows.
--   Money is a NUMBER, in Singapore dollars.
--   A date is written Date day month year (never year first), from IMPORT daydate.
--   A period is counted only by sg-periods.l4; no part writes its own date arithmetic.
--   A name that begins "s " or "sch " belongs to the provision it implements; the names below do not,
--   so a part's name can never collide with one of these.
--
-- Membership test: could a witness of ordinary competence testify to the fact,
-- or does answering it need the Act? Only the first kind is here.

§ `The people and bodies the Act names`

-- The party of a regulative rule, and the word for who a fact is about.
-- The first five and `Member`, `Creditor`, `Auditor` are people or companies and carry a name.
-- The last four are offices of the State: they appear only as what they mean to the individual
-- (the encoding has no seat for them), and carry no name.
DECLARE Party IS ONE OF
    Individual HAS `the name of the person` IS A STRING      -- a natural person: the individual in the seat, or anyone else
    Company    HAS `the name of the company` IS A STRING      -- a company incorporated under the Act
    Director   HAS `the name of the director` IS A STRING     -- a person occupying the position of director of a company
    Officer    HAS `the name of the officer` IS A STRING      -- an officer of a corporation (a director, the secretary, an executive)
    Secretary  HAS `the name of the secretary` IS A STRING    -- the secretary of a company
    Member     HAS `the name of the member` IS A STRING       -- a member (shareholder) of a company
    Creditor   HAS `the name of the creditor` IS A STRING     -- a creditor of a company
    Auditor    HAS `the name of the auditor` IS A STRING      -- the person or entity appointed as a company's auditor
    Registrar                                                 -- the Registrar of Companies
    Minister                                                  -- the Minister
    Court                                                     -- the Court (the General Division of the High Court)
    Authority                                                 -- the Accounting and Corporate Regulatory Authority

-- A corporation, known by its name. Groups (ss 5 to 6) are lists of these and of links between them (sg-groups.l4).
DECLARE Corporation HAS
    `the name of the corporation` IS A STRING

§ `The kinds of company and the things a company has`

-- How far the members' liability goes (s 4(1) "company limited by shares", "company limited by guarantee",
-- "unlimited company", "limited company"). A company limited both by shares and by guarantee
-- exists only until the end of the period in s 17(6) ("limited company").
DECLARE `Liability of members` IS ONE OF
    `limited by shares`
    `limited by guarantee`
    `limited by shares and by guarantee`
    `unlimited`

-- Whether a company is private or public is not here: it is a rule (s 4(1) "private company",
-- "public company", "exempt private company"), asked as the input `the company is a private company`.

-- The kinds of share a rule names.
DECLARE `Kind of share` IS ONE OF
    `an ordinary share`
    `a preference share`
    `a redeemable preference share`
    `a treasury share`

-- A class of shares: the shares carrying the same rights.
DECLARE `Class of shares` HAS
    `the name of the class` IS A STRING
    `the kind of share in the class` IS A `Kind of share`
    `the number of issued shares in the class` IS A NUMBER

-- The kinds of resolution and of meeting the Act refers to.
DECLARE `Kind of resolution` IS ONE OF
    `an ordinary resolution`
    `a special resolution`
    `a resolution of the directors`

DECLARE `Kind of meeting` IS ONE OF
    `an annual general meeting`
    `an extraordinary general meeting`
    `the statutory meeting`
    `a meeting of a class of members`
    `a meeting of creditors`

§ `The solvency statement (s 7A)`

-- The three proposals for which the Act asks the directors for a solvency statement (s 7A(1)).
-- The last constructor is every other proposal: s 7A(1) defines the term only "in relation to" the three.
DECLARE `Proposal needing a solvency statement` IS ONE OF
    `a redemption of preference shares out of capital under section 70`
    `a giving of financial assistance under section 76(9A) or (9B)`
    `a reduction of share capital under section 78B or 78C`
    `some other proposal`

-- What a solvency statement SAYS and how it was made out: facts a witness can read off the document.
-- The rule that decides whether it is one is sg-solvency.l4; this record carries no rule.
DECLARE `Solvency statement` HAS
    `the proposal it concerns` IS A `Proposal needing a solvency statement`
    `the date of the statement` IS A DATE
    `it is a statement by the directors of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it says the directors have formed the opinion that, as regards the company's situation at its date, there is no ground on which the company could then be found to be unable to pay its debts` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it says the directors have formed the opinion that the company will be able to pay its debts in full within 12 months after the commencement of winding up` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it says the directors have formed the opinion that the company will be able to pay its debts as they fall due during the 12 months immediately after its date` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it says the directors have formed the opinion that the value of the company's assets is not less than the value of its liabilities (including contingent liabilities)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it says the directors have formed the opinion that the value of the company's assets will not, after the proposal, become less than the value of its liabilities (including contingent liabilities)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the directors intend to commence winding up of the company within the 12 months immediately after its date` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the number of directors of the company` IS A NUMBER
    `the number of directors who have signed it as a written declaration` IS A NUMBER
    `it is accompanied by a report from the company's auditor that the auditor has inquired into the affairs of the company and is of the opinion that the statement is not unreasonable given all the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN

§ `Dates the Act itself names`

-- s 3(2)(a) and s 4(1) "private company" (a): "immediately before 29 December 1967".
`the day 29 December 1967` MEANS Date 29 12 1967

-- s 4(1) "constitution" (b) and s 4(13): "3 January 2016", the day memoranda and articles became constitutions.
`the day 3 January 2016` MEANS Date 3 1 2016
